From 1a069cd832481cc1c169287aa9c41d9f384294c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 14:05:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Design system: reversed logo for dark grounds

- logos/happycynic-logo-reversed.svg and .png: the full lockup with a
  white wordmark; "SOFTWARE" stays teal and the face is unchanged. The
  PNG is the existing PNG with the black wordmark pixels set to white
  (alpha kept), so it keeps the original Helvetica rendering.
- README and logos/README: use the reversed logo on dark grounds; the
  face alone remains for tight spaces.
- SiteHeader: a third image, .hc-logo--reversed, shown in the dark
  theme. Headers without it keep falling back to the face alone.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TqzRgBTn3vSvbb1swBihtT
