diff --git a/design-system/README.md b/design-system/README.md
index 02edf3c..e1fbfbe 100644
--- a/design-system/README.md
+++ b/design-system/README.md
@@ -46,7 +46,7 @@ Real copy to calibrate against:
 The logo has two parts: the **face** (`happycynic-icon`) and the **wordmark** "Happy Cynic / SOFTWARE". Files live in [`logos/`](logos/).
 
 - Use the **full logo** (`happycynic-logo.svg` or `.png`) on `surface` or `surface-raised` in the light theme. Its wordmark is black (`logo-ink`), so it does not work on dark grounds.
-- On dark grounds (`surface` in dark, `surface-inverse`), use the **face alone** (`happycynic-icon`); its built-in white disc keeps it legible. Do not invert or recolor the wordmark yourself.
+- On dark grounds (`surface` in dark, `surface-inverse`), use the **reversed logo** (`happycynic-logo-reversed.svg` or `.png`): the same lockup with a white wordmark, "SOFTWARE" still `teal`. Where space is tight, the **face alone** (`happycynic-icon`) works on any ground. Never invert or recolor the logo yourself; use these files.
 - Clear space: at least a quarter of the face's height on every side. Minimum size: full logo 120px wide, face 16px (use the purpose-made `favicon-16.png` / `favicon-32.png` at those sizes).
 - Never recolor the halves, swap their sides, separate them, rotate the mark, add a shadow or outline, or place it on a busy photo.
 - The SVG wordmark keeps "SOFTWARE" as live Helvetica text. On systems without Helvetica (Windows, Android, some browsers), use the PNG.
diff --git a/design-system/components/SiteHeader/README.md b/design-system/components/SiteHeader/README.md
index b521d23..39724f6 100644
--- a/design-system/components/SiteHeader/README.md
+++ b/design-system/components/SiteHeader/README.md
@@ -2,11 +2,11 @@
 
 The happycynic.com masthead: the full logo centred above a short, pipe-separated nav on `surface-raised` with `shadow-md`.
 
-**Markup:** `<header class="hc-header">` holding `.hc-header__logo` (two images: `.hc-logo--full` and `.hc-logo--face`) and `<nav class="hc-nav">` with links separated by `<span class="hc-nav__sep" aria-hidden="true">|</span>`. Mark the current page with `aria-current="page"`.
+**Markup:** `<header class="hc-header">` holding `.hc-header__logo` (three images: `.hc-logo--full`, `.hc-logo--reversed` and `.hc-logo--face`) and `<nav class="hc-nav">` with links separated by `<span class="hc-nav__sep" aria-hidden="true">|</span>`. Mark the current page with `aria-current="page"`.
 
-**Compact variant:** add `hc-header--compact` to the header: the logo sits left at 60px (face 48px in dark), the nav right without separators, wrapping under the logo on phones. Leave out the `hc-nav__sep` spans; a small primary `Button` (for example GitHub) and a `ThemeToggle` may end the nav.
+**Compact variant:** add `hc-header--compact` to the header: the logo sits left at 60px, the nav right without separators, wrapping under the logo on phones. Leave out the `hc-nav__sep` spans; a small primary `Button` (for example GitHub) and a `ThemeToggle` may end the nav.
 
 - Keep the nav to three to five Title Case items.
 - One layout per site: centred for a one-page site, compact once it has several sections.
-- Both logo images are required: the dark theme hides the full logo (its wordmark is black) and shows the face alone.
+- The dark theme swaps the full logo (black wordmark) for `.hc-logo--reversed` (`happycynic-logo-reversed`). A header without the reversed image falls back to `.hc-logo--face`, the face alone.
 - Product sites use their own header; this one is for Happy Cynic properties.
diff --git a/design-system/components/bundle.css b/design-system/components/bundle.css
index 7e36d17..ccfa318 100644
--- a/design-system/components/bundle.css
+++ b/design-system/components/bundle.css
@@ -136,7 +136,8 @@
   gap: var(--space-4) var(--space-6);
   padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-6);
 }
-.hc-header--compact .hc-header__logo .hc-logo--full { height: 60px; }
+.hc-header--compact .hc-header__logo .hc-logo--full,
+.hc-header--compact .hc-header__logo .hc-logo--reversed { height: 60px; }
 .hc-header--compact .hc-header__logo .hc-logo--face { height: 48px; }
 .hc-header--compact .hc-nav { margin-top: 0; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--space-6); }
 
@@ -212,7 +213,11 @@
   .hc-btn, .hc-nav a, .hc-theme-toggle { transition: none; }
 }
 
-/* The full logo's wordmark is black: on dark grounds show the face alone */
-.hc-header__logo .hc-logo--face { display: none; height: 72px; }
+/* The full logo's wordmark is black: on dark grounds show the reversed logo,
+   or the face alone in a header that has no reversed image */
+.hc-header__logo .hc-logo--face,
+.hc-header__logo .hc-logo--reversed { display: none; }
+.hc-header__logo .hc-logo--face { height: 72px; }
 [data-theme="dark"] .hc-header__logo .hc-logo--full { display: none; }
-[data-theme="dark"] .hc-header__logo .hc-logo--face { display: block; }
+[data-theme="dark"] .hc-header__logo .hc-logo--reversed { display: block; }
+[data-theme="dark"] .hc-header__logo:not(:has(.hc-logo--reversed)) .hc-logo--face { display: block; }
diff --git a/design-system/logos/README.md b/design-system/logos/README.md
index 8c6c021..4744a9e 100644
--- a/design-system/logos/README.md
+++ b/design-system/logos/README.md
@@ -3,7 +3,8 @@
 The official Happy Cynic marks, exported from the master Illustrator file.
 
 - `happycynic-logo.svg` / `.png` — the full lockup: face plus "Happy Cynic / SOFTWARE". Light grounds only (`surface`, `surface-raised` in light). The wordmark ink is `logo-ink` (#000000); "SOFTWARE" is `teal` (#27a4a3). In the SVG, "SOFTWARE" is live Helvetica text (falling back to Arial): prefer the PNG where Helvetica may be missing. Both SVGs carry their colours as inline `fill` attributes rather than a `<style>` block, so they survive sanitisers and render the same everywhere.
+- `happycynic-logo-reversed.svg` / `.png` — the full lockup for dark grounds (`surface` and `surface-raised` in dark, `surface-inverse`): the wordmark is white (#ffffff), "SOFTWARE" stays `teal` (#27a4a3, 6:1 on dark `surface`), the face is unchanged. Same proportions, clear space and minimum size as the full logo; the same Helvetica caveat applies to the SVG, so prefer the PNG.
 - `happycynic-icon.svg` / `.png` — the face alone: `sunny` (#ffda3c) left, `teal` (#27a4a3) right, `logo-ink` outline on a white disc. Works on light and dark grounds. Use for avatars, app icons, social profiles and the `Endorsement`.
 - `favicon-32.png`, `favicon-16.png` — pixel-tuned face for browser tabs. Use only at those exact sizes.
 
-Not yet available: a reversed (white) wordmark for dark grounds, a single-color version for engraving or fax-style use, and a horizontal lockup.
+Not yet available: a single-color version for engraving or fax-style use, and a horizontal lockup.
